Z||000006||wkayl||10-06-2000||07:12 PM||||When my son wanted to get his 1st car he wanted a Comaro or a Mustang.  When he saw a Fiero for sale he felt just like you.  And I didn't know if I wanted him to have one either.  I didn't own mine at that time (I liked his so well that I had to have one).  After looking at one I made the following observations:<P>Cost of 84 SE=he could afford to buy his own car<P>Sporty=no razzing from friends<P>4 cyl=not lots of power to spin the tires<P>4 cyl=good gas milage<P>Automatic=tire spinning same as above<P>Automatic=good for novice driver<P>2 seater=if friends want to cruise, they drive<P>2 seater=no more than 1 friend yelling "pass him...pass him..."<P>High center console=guy on guy side and girl on girl side<P>High center console=guy on guy side and girl on girl side<P>One negative for you would be Dad may want to drive it as much as you do.||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||10-06-2000||07:24 PM||||i agree with all of the above. <P>assumeing that dear old dad meands the coolant pipes at the back... i have never seen them cut, but did see them crushed in one car.  my guess was that the mechanic that put it on the lift didnt know what he was doing.<P>i have owned my car for 11 years, and have no problems with the coolant pipes.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||frontal lobe||10-06-2000||07:35 PM||||Your dad should be easy to convince:<P>1.  You are a girl.<P>2.  No back seat.<P>Case closed.||||reg||1
