Z||000026||Oreif||10-07-2000||10:46 AM||||We had a local club member who was T-boned (hit in the side) at about 45 mph by a full sized Chevy Pick-up truck. He was wearing his seatbelt and the car slpit in half. But he walked away with minor aches and scratches. (Unfortunately the driver of the truck did not believe in seatbelts and spent 6 weeks in the hospitol after bouncing off the windshield of his truck.<BR>You can read the article from the person who was driving the Fiero at:<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/art-wreck.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/art-wreck.html</A> <P>Also the Fiero was second best car in crash tests. (Volvo was #1)<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||Seanh||10-07-2000||12:25 PM||||Wow, thats a bad accident. I hear that kind of thing all the time about trucks and SUV's. When I go with friends who drive SUV's and trucks, I get in and put my seat belt on, they tell me not to bother because I wouldnt get hurt in a truck or SUV, there just as safe without wearing a seat belt.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000028||Raydar||10-07-2000||12:44 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>...unless you're one of those people that can break a crowbar in a sandbox......<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ROFL!!<BR>I know some people like that.<P>Xfilesgirl1,<BR>Good luck. I think that your dad and you will both be pleased with the Fiero.<BR>BTW... Welcome to Cliff's Fiero Forum.<BR>This group is probably the largest collection of Fiero fanatics in the world.<BR>I have learned tons of stuff, from the folks here. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (soon to receive transplant.)<BR>88 "pretzeled" Formula <P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-07-2000).]||||reg||1
